title The derivation tree, and the wrong sentence it found beneath itself
prompt Autonomous loop -- pick up the running thread, Standfast on reds first, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Lindy-priority Microkernel Target double-seat, read one council-rota doc, sweep the prose Radiant, send.
think Read the voice and the style before the route, so the whole lap is written in Kyri from the first token. Then REMEMBER, then the double-seat itinerary line 101 where the microkernel's precedence over Seasons A-H is seated on Keaton's word, then the top rows of the log index and the newest recommend. The baton was unambiguous: the derivation tree is the next rung and it is ungated, being the largest of the seven debts the refusal agenda named.
think Standfast first. The corrective queue was emptied before the restart -- %104, %105, %106 all carry closure notes -- so no red stood between the lap and new work. That check costs one grep and it is the difference between building on ground and building on a fault.
think Scoped the rung SLC before writing a line. Simple: one table, one lineage, five operations. Complete: the loop closes -- seat, derive, delete, revoke, and a whole-table invariant that re-proves what the edge checked. Deliberately NOT in scope: untyped retyping, the IPC buffer, and the three edge checks, each of which is its own subsystem in the agenda and would have made this rung large and half-finished rather than small and whole.
think Chose to import the vocabulary rather than restate it. `derivation.rye` answers in `refusals.rye`'s own `KernelRefusal`, so the binding that witness holds against seL4's BSD-2-Clause header at run time carries through to this rung for free. A second copy of the eleven would have been a second place to drift.
think Bounded both dimensions and made the bounds refuse differently from the kernel's answers, on purpose. Thirty-two slots and four deep refuse with named Rye errors, because the kernel offers no word for "the userland's table is full." Blurring those two vocabularies would have quietly claimed the bounds-checking debt this rung does not pay.
think The depth bound is what lets `descends_from` stay a loop rather than a recursion -- a walk up the lineage terminates in a known number of steps. That is TAME's no-unbounded-recursion rule paying for itself in the design rather than being bolted on after.
think Then the module printed its worked tree and the two refusals side by side, and they read as the same sentence. That is what caught REDS %107. `refusals.rye` had shipped `seL4_DeleteFirst` as "a child capability stands beneath this one" -- which is `seL4_RevokeFirst`'s meaning, not its own.
think Went to a source rather than to a memory. seL4's `errors.h` carries names and nothing else, which is exactly why the meanings were unbound. Its interface files carry the descriptions: `libsel4/include/interfaces/object-api.xml`, BSD-2-Clause, already vendored, already licensed to read. Nine occurrences of `seL4_DeleteFirst`, every one saying "The destination slot contains a capability." Unambiguous in one grep.
think Booked the red before fixing it, then fixed it at the root and turned the lantern into a loom. A one-sided check would have held our prose to a phrase we typed; the two-sided binding holds our sentence and the kernel's to each other, so a reword on either side reds the rung. Three of the eleven are bound where seL4 publishes one unambiguous load-bearing sentence, and the eight remaining are counted and reported in the same output line rather than passed over -- REDS %102 taught that a scan quietly narrowing its subject is the deeper fault.
think Gathering the descriptions taught its own small lesson, worth the line it costs. seL4 writes them two ways, as a `description="..."` attribute and as a nested `<description>` element, and stripping tags first deletes the attribute form along with its tag. The first run reported that seL4 no longer publishes a phrase seL4 publishes plainly. Measured it before believing it.
think Proved the RED path with the exact sentence that shipped rather than with an invented one. The plant rewrites `delete_first`'s meaning back to "a child capability stands beneath this one" and the scan refuses it with `ours_missing=1`. A loom that catches its own founding fault is a loom worth keeping.
think For the tree's own RED paths, planted two removals that each take away one thing the tree exists to guarantee -- the attenuation check, so reach could widen as it is handed on, and the whole-lineage sweep, so a grandchild survives its grandparent's revocation. Both copies abort on their own asserts. The copies carry a copy of their imported neighbour so the living tree is never touched.
think The carry meter caught my own module and went RED on its pin, which is the entire reason it stands. Moved all four ladder meters 103 -> 104 and the body and family counts with them, in the same commit as the code -- a meter whose pins lag its subject has stopped guarding. Re-measured twice, since splitting the self-test moved the body count again.
think TAME's seventy-line ratchet named `run_self_test` at 83 lines. It prints rather than fails, yet the rule says migrate on touch in a file you edit, and I authored this file this round. Split it into three movements -- lineage, revoke, bounds -- each of which names what it proves, so the split made the test more legible rather than merely shorter.
think One honest reconciliation rather than a convenient one. `refusals.rye` still counts seven owed even though the tree now answers two, because its count is what the POLICY TABLE can answer and the table above the line has not learned to speak through the tree. Crediting the table with a neighbour's reach would have made the agenda lie in the flattering direction.
think The REDS tally line said 106 rows. Editing it to 107 by hand would have been REDS %93's exact fault, so I reverted that and let the monotone witness read the spine off disk instead -- 107, measured. The tally line now names the witness that produced it and the stamp it was produced at.
obs The rota doc this lap was `context/SIMPLE_LOVABLE_COMPLETE.md`, and it decided the scope before the first line was written. Complete means the loop closes within the bounds the work sets for itself. A derivation tree that also tried to carve untyped memory and bound IPC messages would have been three half-things; one that keeps lineage and answers exactly the two refusals lineage can answer is whole at its scope and claims no more.
obs The deeper lesson of the round is one sentence: a parity check that binds a NAME proves nothing about what the name means. The refusals witness was strong exactly where it looked -- symbol, order, run-time re-read of the vendored header -- and blind one column over, so a wrong claim rode inside a GREEN rung for one lap. This is REDS %102's family in a new dress, where a guard reading a narrower subject than the claim it appears to protect answers the question nobody asked in the voice of the question they did.
obs Building the next rung is the strongest audit of the rung beneath it. Nothing in a reading pass over `refusals.rye` would have surfaced this; writing the two answers as code forced the question of which is which, and the source was already on disk waiting to answer.
obs Five of the seven debts remain, and the IPC buffer is the natural next rung. It is one bounded structure with a named minimum rather than three separate edge checks, so it is the largest single move still standing and it composes with the message-passing the arc will want next anyway.
loom witness=caravan_derivation wall_s=21 slots=32 max_depth=4 refusals_answered=2 refusals_reused=2 named_errors=2 red_paths=2
loom witness=caravan_refusals wall_s=15 meanings_bound=3 meanings_unbound=8 kernel_missing=0 ours_missing=0 red_paths=3
loom witness=caravan_suite wall_s=438 rungs=101 roster_disk=101 roster_registered=101
loom meter=caravan_ladder_carry modules=104 bodies=17996 distinct=7801 copies=10195 carried_lines=137149 families=704
loom witness=reds_ledger_monotone rows=107 mentions=118 gaps_or_dupes=0
file caravan/derivation.rye the rung -- lineage kept, reach narrowing along it, and the two refusals only a tree can answer
file tools/caravan_derivation_witness.rish the proof -- the self-test, the worked tree, and both RED paths planted rather than described
file tools/fixtures/caravan_derivation_control.sh the two plants, in a fixture so the shell owns its quoting (REDS %85's loom)
file caravan/refusals.rye REDS %107 closed at the root -- both meanings corrected against seL4's own published descriptions
file tools/fixtures/caravan_refusal_meaning_scan.sh the loom -- meanings bound two-sidedly, the unbound counted rather than passed over
file tools/caravan_refusals_witness.rish the meaning leg and its RED path, which is REDS %107's own wrong sentence
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish the new rung registered, so the choir's bijection stays whole at 101
file tools/caravan_ladder_carry_witness.rish module pin 103 -> 104, with bodies and families re-measured twice
file tools/caravan_ladder_spine_witness.rish module pin moved in the same commit as the code it measures
file tools/caravan_ladder_print_witness.rish module pin moved in the same commit as the code it measures
file tools/gen/season/reds_ledger_monotone_witness.rish the spine re-pinned at 107, read off disk rather than edited by hand
file crux/REDS.md %107 booked and closed, and the row tally re-measured by the witness that can count it
file caravan/README.md the durable record -- the tree, the correction, and what neither claims
file crux/REMEMBER.md Now refilled with live work; the refusal-vocabulary chronicle folded to a prior-edge pointer
recommend keep-going The IPC buffer is the next rung and it is ungated: it owes `seL4_TruncatedMessage`, it is one bounded structure with a named minimum rather than three separate edge checks, and it composes with the message-passing this arc wants next. The one gate worth Keaton's eye stays small and unchanged -- jinja2 and ply on the pier's Python environment open five more libsel4 headers in a single step.
